{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is scored exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. The context inputs `x`, `x0`, `N`, `N_grid`, and `x_grid` are not protected because they are used only as predictors, sizes, or generated-quantity inputs. Each parameter has exactly one built-in prior before it is used in the likelihood.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  real x0; // Baseline input

  int<lower=1> N; // Number of observations
  vector[N] x; // Observed inputs
  vector[N] y; // Observed outputs

  int<lower=1> N_grid; // Number of grid points
  array[N_grid] real x_grid;  // Input grid
}

parameters {
  real alpha; // Intercept
  real beta;  // Slope
  real<lower=0> sigma; // Measurement Variability
}

model {
  alpha ~ normal(0, 3);
  beta ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 1);

  y ~ normal(alpha + beta * (x - x0), sigma);
}

generated quantities {
  array[N] real y_pred;
  array[N_grid] real mu_grid;
  array[N_grid] real y_pred_grid;

  for (n in 1:N)
    y_pred[n] = normal_rng(alpha + beta * (x[n] - x0), sigma);

  for (n in 1:N_grid) {
    mu_grid[n] = alpha + beta * (x_grid[n] - x0);
    y_pred_grid[n] = normal_rng(mu_grid[n], sigma);
  }
}

